083 - O Worship the King
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 83
Topic: God the Father - 

Verse 1:
[G]O worship [D]the [G]King, all [C]glorious [G]a[D]bove,
[D7]O[G]grateful[D]ly [G]sing [C]His [G]wonder[D7]ful [G]love;
[D]Our shield and [A7]de[D7]fender, [G]the [D]Ancient [G]of [D7]days,
[D7]Pa[G]vilioned [D]in [G]splendour, [D]and [G]girded [D7]with [G]praise.

Verse 2:
[G]O [D]tell of [G]His might, [C]O [G]sing of [D]His grace,
[D7]Whose [G]robe [D]is [G]the [C]light, [G]whose [D7]canopy [G]space,
[D]His [A7]chariots [D7]of [G]wrath [D]the [G]deep [D7]thunderclouds form,
[D7]And [G]dark [D]is His [G]path [D]on [G]the wings [D7]of [G]the storm.

Verse 3:
[G]Thy [D]bountiful [G]care, [C]what [G]tongue [D]can recite?
[D7]It [G]breathes [D]in [G]the air, [C]it [G]shines [D7]in [G]the light;
[D]It [A7]streams [D7]from the [G]hills, [D]it descends [G]to [D7]the plain,
[D7]And [G]sweetly [D]distills [G]in [D]the [G]dew [D7]and [G]the rain.

Verse 4:
[G]Frail [D]children [G]of dust, [C]and [G]feeble [D]as frail,
[D7]In [G]Thee [D]do [G]we trust, [C]nor [G]find [D7]Thee [G]to fail;
[D]Thy [A7]mercies [D7]how [G]tender, how [D]firm [G]to [D7]the end!
[D7][G]Our [D]Maker, [G]Defender, [D][G]Redeemer, [D7]and [G]Friend.
